    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d103">

                <pb facs="0216" n="168" sameAs="frus:frus1877/pg168"/>

                <head>No. 103.<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Hitt to Mr. Evarts.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Legation of the United States</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Paris</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1877-08-20"><hi rendition="#italic">August</hi> 20, 1877</date>.
                        (Received September 7.)</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 1523.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have the honor to transmit herewith three
                    copies of a circular received from Mr. Berger, director of the foreign sections
                    of the Universal Exposition of 1878, and which has been sent to all the
                    commissions of foreign countries, giving much information in regard to the state
                    of advancement of the work, and urging prompt action on the part of the
                    commissions.</p>
                <p>You will remark the important statement that the essential parts of the
                    exposition buildings will be completed by the 15th of September, and the laying
                    of the floors between then and the 1st of October, when the commission of each
                    country can proceed to parcel out its section.</p>
                <p>I have, &amp;c.,</p>
                <closer><signed>R. R. HITT.</signed></closer>


                <xi:include href="d103-a1.xml" xpointer="d103-a1"/>
            </div>
        </body>
